## Specifics

* **What is a server?**
  A server is a physical or virtual machine (or software program) designed to provide services, functionality, or resources to other computers or programs called "clients".

* **What is the role of the domain name?**
  A domain name provides a human-readable, user-friendly address (e.g., `foobar.com`) to locate internet resources, replacing numeric IP addresses that are difficult to remember.

* **What type of DNS record `www` is in `www.foobar.com`?**
  It is typically configured as a **CNAME record** pointing `www.foobar.com` to the apex domain `foobar.com` (which points to `8.8.8.8`), or an **A record** mapping directly to `8.8.8.8`.

* **What is the role of the web server (Nginx)?**
  It handles incoming HTTP/HTTPS requests from clients, directly serves static assets, and acts as a reverse proxy by forwarding dynamic requests to the application server.

* **What is the role of the application server?**
  It executes the dynamic application code and business logic, processes incoming parameters, communicates with the database, and builds dynamic content to send back to the web server.

* **What is the role of the database (MySQL)?**
  It stores, organizes, and manages persistent and structured application data, providing fast querying and data retrieval capabilities.

* **What is the server using to communicate with the computer of the user requesting the website?**
  It uses the **TCP/IP** protocol suite over the internet, transmitting application data specifically through the **HTTP** protocol (port 80) or **HTTPS** (port 443).

