## Issues with this infrastructure

* **Single Point of Failure (SPOF):**
  Since all core components (Nginx, application server, and MySQL database) reside on one server, any hardware failure, network outage, or OS crash results in total website downtime.

* **Downtime when maintenance is needed:**
  Performing system updates, restarting Nginx/MySQL, or deploying new code updates requires taking services offline temporarily, causing service interruption for visitors.

* **Cannot scale if there is too much incoming traffic:**
  A single server can only scale vertically (by upgrading CPU/RAM), which has hardware and cost boundaries. Spikes in web traffic can exhaust available resources, causing the server to freeze or crash.
